ders 601 and 786, close to expected demand.\n- **Candidate 6:** orders 693 of product 0, about 115 extra. That means more holding cost and some stock expiring.\n- **Candidate 7:** orders 868 of product 1, about 90 extra, with the same downside.\n\n**Robustness to random demand.**\n- **Candidate 1:** product 0 arrives on even days and product 1 on odd days. The largest single delivery is 121 units, so the warehouse never overflows. The 121 units of product 1 arrive on day 11, just before the demand spike on day 12 (82 units).\n- **3-day plans:** both products arrive on the same day, about 180–200 units at once plus leftover stock. When demand runs low, the 216-unit limit can be exceeded and product 1 is lost on arrival.\n- **Leftovers:** in every plan they carry over to the next cycle, because shelf life is 7–9 days. That makes a small surplus cheap, while a missing unit of product 0 costs 10 (8 lost margin plus 2 penalty).\n\nCandidate 1 orders 4 more times than candidate 3, costing about 190 extra. It saves about 310 on holding and avoids the overflow risk. Overall it comes out roughly 100–150 ahead of the best 3-day plan (candidate 3)."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 355, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5754, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 355}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-26T08:32:12.212Z", "request_id": "req_011CgQY6tBwDSUf2Gj3d9j6o"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01BUUEUahk4ULepyDHdyuZuu", "name": "Structu